        "text": "Standard agent Signed agent (0.27+) Standard (Linux) (0.32+) Standard (macOS) (0.33+) RustDesk only : Linux before 0.32, macOS before 0.33 or without Quick Connect What it is The Windows install script's scheduled tasks (update channel ) The signed , installed from the signed update channel ( ) A POSIX script and a systemd timer, installed by the Linux installer; read only A POSIX script and a LaunchDaemon in , installed by the macOS installer run with ; read only RustDesk plus a one time registration at install A one off RustDesk session, nothing installed Remote access (RustDesk, launch policy, audit) Yes Yes Yes Yes Yes Yes, for that session Heartbeat, online/offline Yes Yes Yes, every 3 minutes, with the device secret Yes, every 3 minutes, with the device secret At install only No Inventory (hardware, OS, disks, last boot) Yes Yes Yes: os release, kernel, uptime, CPU model and load, memory, disks ( ), logged on users ( ), DMI where readable Yes: , kernel, boot time ( ), CPU model and load ( ), memory ( ), volumes ( , ), console user, model and serial ( , ) No No Installed software and change history (0.29) Yes Yes No No No No Windows event log reading Yes Yes No (a staged query is refused) No (a staged query is refused) No No One click read only diagnostics (0.31): disk, services, errors, processes, network, DNS, updates, restart Yes Yes (the same heartbeat script) No No No No Metric history (0.33): CPU, memory, system disk per heartbeat; each volume per inventory pass Yes Yes Yes Yes No No Processes, Services and Network tabs (0.33): full read only snapshots Yes Yes (the same heartbeat script) No (its agent reads no diagnostics) No (its agent reads no diagnostics) No No Monitoring (offline, disk, CPU, memory, services, events, restart pending) Yes Yes Offline, system disk, CPU, memory and restart pending, from the values it reports; no services or events Offline, system disk, CPU and memory; no services, events or restart pending Offline only (it stops heartbeating) No Patches: pending updates, restart pending Yes — read only , every 12 h or on Scan now Yes Yes — read only : , or , from the package manager's existing cache; unknown with none of them Yes — read only : the list macOS itself last found ( ), never ; unknown if macOS has not checked within 36 hours. Restart pending: always unknown No No Patches: update identities, history, restart sources No Yes No No No No Patches: who manages patching (WSUS, Intune, WUfB, ConfigMgr) No — shown as Unknown Yes No — shown as Unknown No — shown as Unknown No No Patches: confirmed by a later scan No Yes No No No No Deploying updates (canary, rings, two approvals) No Yes, when approvals are configured No No No No Approved actions (start the Print Spooler) No Yes, when approvals are configured No No No No Maintenance actions (restart an allowlisted service, schedule or cancel a restart, collect logs) No Yes (0.32+ agent), when approvals are configured No No No No Chat with the person at the computer (0.34; chat.md) No Yes (0.34+ agent; not yet run on real Windows ) No No No No Password rotation, reinstall, RustDesk client update from the console Yes Yes No — the console refuses them; re run the installer on the computer No — the console refuses them; re run the installer on the computer No No Agent card (0.34): type, version, current or behind, channel, portal update mode, last update result Yes Yes (last update result from 0.34 signed builds) Yes, with the command to re run the installer Yes, with the command to re run the installer Type only No Update agent from the console (0.34) Yes: re runs the current standard installer (the reinstall path) Check for update now : , signed files only No — re run the installer on the computer No — re run the installer on the computer No No Upgrade to signed agent from the console, one computer or a selection (0.34) Yes, with a fresh sign in and a reason, while the portal is not in Signed only ; fixture tested only Already signed No signed agent"
