        "heading": "Patch status on the Patches tab (0.30)",
        "id": "patch-status-on-the-patches-tab-030",
        "text": "Every computer's Patches tab now leads with Patch status : the evidence first, then what follows from it. Field Where it comes from Evidence Signed agent scan , Standard agent scan (read only) or No scan received , with its time, its age and fresh / stale / unknown . Stale means older than 36 hours: three missed 12 hour scans Last successful scan A signed scan that came back with an error is not a successful scan Last boot The inventory's last boot time Connection Online, or offline since when Restart pending From the scan; unknown when nothing was received, never \"no\" Who manages patching WSUS , MDM (Intune) update policy , Windows Update for Business policy or Configuration Manager , with what that means, when the signed agent finds them. Unknown from the standard agent, which does not read update policy. Windows Update (rem0te can deploy) when the signed agent found none Relevant KBs The KB numbers offered, critical and important first Installed by an approved plan Each update from a recent plan, and whether a later scan confirmed it. Only a scan taken after the install, which no longer offers the update, shows no restart pending and has Windows Update's history recording it, counts Deploy from rem0te Available, or why not: no signed agent, managed elsewhere, no signed scan yet, or the scan is stale WSUS and Intune ownership. When a computer takes its updates from WSUS (Group Policy with ) or from an Intune update ring (the policy), approvals and timing belong to that system. Rem0te shows what the computer reports and will not deploy there. The signed agent refuses too, so the two never fight over a computer. In a linked ticket. When a restart pending alert is offered to ClientSt0r, it carries a redacted summary (contract revision 2, ): evidence source and age, freshness, last boot, who manages patching (as a label), restart pending, the pending KB numbers, and which KBs were confirmed, failed or are awaiting confirmation. It never carries update titles, error text, computer identifiers, user names, addresses or registry values."
