        "text": "Every result is re shaped field by field before it is stored ( ): unknown fields dropped, strings clamped and stripped of control characters, profile paths and long opaque tokens redacted, numbers range checked, lists cut (50 error groups, 10 processes, 16 adapters…), and the whole result capped at 32 KB — 128 KB for the three snapshot keys, which list everything. A run is only updated by the computer it was staged for, under its own key. keeps only the monitored services this server asked about. and go through the inventory service exactly as the automatic collections do, and the run keeps a summary. The catalog is closed in four places: the request (unknown key: 400 ), the heartbeat, the result, and the database — has a constraint listing the twelve keys (migration 0042 added the snapshots), and results over 64 KB (256 KB for a snapshot) are refused by another. Adding a diagnostic is a migration on purpose. §20 checks all of it, and §31 the snapshots. Who may see what. Every route here applies business scope and the device list visibility rule: a Business User sees only the computers granted to them (or marked company wide), and any other computer — in their business or not — reads as missing (404). Before 0.33 only business scope was checked here, so such a user could stage a run on a computer they could not see (it then failed at delivery) and read that computer's run history. Audit. (who, which key, the run) and (outcome completed, failed or expired, size, whether truncated) — never result content. A result posted with the wrong device secret is , reason ."
