        "text": "Reports Reports (in the menu from 0.32) answer four questions over a business, a site and a period, from data Rem0te really stores. Nothing on these pages is estimated, sampled or filled in: a figure with no evidence behind it says No data , and an empty report says what is missing. Report Answers Needs Patch compliance Which devices are up to date with Windows Update, per business and site, and which have no current scan View computers Agent coverage Which agent each device runs and at what version; devices without a device secret; devices not heard from in N days; non Windows devices with no inventory View computers Alert frequency How many alerts each business, site, computer and monitor type raised in a period, and how long they took to resolve monitoring:alerts Offline time How long computers were unreachable, from the offline episodes the Offline monitor recorded monitoring:alerts Software compliance (0.34) For each software catalog entry, how many Windows computers are compliant, outdated, missing or unknown View computers Each report shows only what you can already see elsewhere: Devices are the ones on your device list: a Business User sees only the computers granted to them (and company wide ones), a technician only their assignment's. Alerts are the ones on your Alerts page, and in addition only on computers you can see. A site outage alert, which belongs to no computer, is in an owner's or technician's report but never a Business User's. Archived and not yet enrolled devices are not counted, as on the dashboard. Alerts raised on a device that was archived later are still counted in alert frequency: they happened. A business you cannot address is refused (403), never answered with an empty report. Filters: Business (a Platform Admin, or anyone who works in several), Site , and for the alert reports a Period (24 hours, 7, 30, 90 or 365 days). Agent coverage has its own Not heard from in choice (1 to 90 days). The filters stay in the address bar, so a report can be bookmarked; whoever opens the link sees it with their own permissions. 1. The reports — one tab each. 2. Offline time — the one the next screenshot opens. 3. Business — then Site; the filters stay in the address bar. 4. Export CSV — the report as on screen, with the same visibility. 5. The totals — each a count of devices, with No data where there is no scan to count from."
