        "heading": "Patch compliance",
        "id": "patch-compliance",
        "text": "The definition is the dashboard's, from the same code ( ), so the two cannot disagree: A device is up to date when its latest Windows Update scan is under 36 hours old and lists no pending updates. Compliance counts only devices with such a scan; coverage is how many devices have one. So a device with a stale scan or none at all is a coverage gap : it is not counted as compliant or as non compliant, because nothing current is known about it. Per business and per site the report shows devices, compliance, up to date over fresh scans, devices needing updates, coverage, stale scans, no scan, and restarts pending (from fresh scans). No scan includes devices that are not Windows, which have no Windows Update to scan; the report says how many. The scan is the signed agent's patch scan when there is one, otherwise the standard agent's 12 hourly update scan. Both are read only evidence; see Staged patching and the device's Patches tab. Below the tables, every device that is not up to date (needing updates first, then stale scans, then no scan) links to its Patches tab."
