        "id": "parameters",
        "text": "A version declares up to 10 parameters, each with a name, a type and limits: Type Limits A charset ( , , , letters, digits, space and ) and a maximum length (1–256) Minimum and maximum (32 bit) — 1–20 fixed values, each an identifier Charsets are a closed list, not author supplied regular expressions, so the portal, the signer and the agent (TypeScript and Go) apply exactly the same rule. Every argument key must be declared (exact name), every required parameter present, and nothing is coerced: is not an integer."
