        "heading": "Data retention",
        "id": "",
        "text": "Data retention Added in 0.34. Before 0.34 nothing that grows was ever pruned: commands, inventory changes, alerts and diagnostics accumulated at about 1.3 MB per computer per year (server sizing.md). The retention sweep now ages out operational history and transient rows on a schedule. The audit log is never pruned. Every table that grows with time falls into one of three kinds: Evidence is kept for ever. Retention never deletes or changes it. Operational history ages out after a window you can configure. Transient rows only mean something until they expire, and are removed some time after that. Settings → System status → Data retention (Platform Admin only) lists each table with its real row count, its oldest row, its window and what removes it. The counts are taken when the page loads and are cached for a minute. The refresh button recounts."
